fice/word/2020/wordml/sdtdatahash" xmlns:w16sdtfl="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2024/wordml/sdtformatlock" xmlns:w16se="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2015/wordml/symex" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 w15 w16se w16cid w16 w16cex w16sdtdh w16sdtfl w16du wp14"><w:body><w:p w14:paraId="7D0767DB" w14:textId="30F7A7A6" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="002B1955" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r w:rsidRPr="002B1955"><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Title:</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00D75768"><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve"> Equipment Asset Tracker System</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="202847A1" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="00000000" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r><w:pict w14:anchorId="4BB56CC6"><v:rect id="_x0000_i1025" style="width:783.3pt;height:.75pt" o:hrpct="0" o:hralign="center" o:hrstd="t" o:hr="t" fillcolor="#a0a0a0" stroked="f"/></w:pict></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4450A3C2" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="002B1955" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r w:rsidRPr="002B1955"><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Objective:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="7D6130CE" w14:textId="55BA1CAE" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="00F325FB" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r w:rsidRPr="00F325FB"><w:t>The objective of this project is to build a fast, self-contained desktop application to comprehensively track and manage organizational hardware. By replacing manual spreadsheets with a secure, offline database, the system provides administrators with real-time visibility into asset availability and user assignments. It automates the entire equipment lifecycle by enforcing strict check-out and check-in workflows, calculating borrowing costs, preventing scheduling conflicts, and logging maintenance repairs. Ultimately, this software aims to eliminate equipment loss and enforce borrower accountability through a reliable, centralized local platform.</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00000000"><w:pict w14:anchorId="0A1AB3D6"><v:rect id="_x0000_i1026" style="width:783.3pt;height:.75pt" o:hrpct="0" o:hralign="center" o:hrstd="t" o:hr="t" fillcolor="#a0a0a0" stroked="f"/></w:pict></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="149A5B68" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="002B1955" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r w:rsidRPr="002B1955"><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Rationale:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="30B0D4FA" w14:textId="1F2D7D9E" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="00F325FB" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:r w:rsidRPr="00F325FB"><w:t>Many organizations struggle to track valuable hardware using messy spreadsheets or overcomplicated cloud applications. Cloud systems often introduce unnecessary hosting fees, require constant internet access, and expose internal data to external servers. A dedicated Windows desktop application solves this by running locally, ensuring instant performance and offline data privacy. Furthermore, by utilizing an embedded SQLite database, the system is completely plug-and-play and requires no complex IT server configurations. This provides a zero-friction, unified environment to manage inventory, audit borrower history, and track repairs seamlessly from a single computer.</w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="00000000"><w:pict w14:anchorId="3D71CC4B"><v:rect id="_x0000_i1027" style="width:783.3pt;height:.75pt" o:hrpct="0" o:hralign="center" o:hrstd="t" o:hr="t" fillcolor="#a0a0a0" stroked="f"/></w:pict></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="17CFCBB7" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="002B1955" w:rsidRPr="002B1955" w:rsidRDefault="002B1955" w:rsidP="002B1955"><w:pPr><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr></w:pPr